    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Martin O'Connor Estate Agents are delighted to offer for sale 'An Crucán', a charming detached bungalow set amidst the breathtaking landscapes of Connemara at An Gort Mór, Rosmuck, Co. Galway. Occupying a peaceful, elevated setting with beautiful views across the surrounding countryside towards the nearby lake and the iconic Twelve Bens mountain range, this is a home that perfectly captures the tranquillity and natural beauty for which the region is renowned.Lovingly maintained over the years, the property offers bright, comfortable accommodation comprising an entrance porch, welcoming entrance hallway, living room, kitchen/dining room, utility room, three bedrooms (1 en- suite), and a family bathroom.Standing on mature, beautifully maintained gardens, the property enjoys excellent privacy together with generous off-street parking and a detached garage, ideal for additional storage, a workshop or a variety of other uses. The elevated site enhances the wonderful outlook, creating a peaceful setting where the ever-changing Connemara landscape can be enjoyed throughout the seasons.Perfectly positioned between the thriving Connemara communities of Rosmuck, Cashel, Cill Chiaráin and Carna, the property combines rural tranquillity with everyday convenience. Cill Chiaráin is approximately a 10-minute drive away and offers an excellent range of local amenities including a primary school, shops, pub and bistro, health centre, playground, astroturf pitch, pier and community hall. Ionad Cultúrtha an Phiarsaigh is located directly across the road from the house. It was here that Patrick Pearse, leader of the 1916 rebellion against British rule, built a summer cottage for himself.Carraroe is approximately 25 minutes away, while the vibrant Irish-speaking village of Carna, renowned for its spectacular Atlantic coastline and secluded beaches, is just 12 miles from the property. The picturesque harbour village of Roundstone, home to the world-famous Dog's Bay and Gurteen beaches, is approximately 23.7 km away, offering some of the most breathtaking coastal scenery along the Wild Atlantic Way.Whether seeking a peaceful permanent residence, a holiday retreat or an investment in one of Ireland's most scenic locations, An Crucan presents a rare opportunity to embrace the unique lifestyle that Connemara has to offer.This property must be seen to be fully appreciated contact DNG Martin O'Connor today to arrange a viewing!"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Porch - \nA welcoming entrance porch with glazed double doors leads into the main hallway.\n\nEntrance Hallway - \nA bright entrance hallway provides access to the main accommodation and creates a warm first impression.\n\nLiving Room - \nA bright and comfortable living room with a large picture window overlooking the surrounding countryside. Featuring an open fireplace with a marble surround and built-in display units, it offers a cosy space to relax.\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nA spacious kitchen and dining room fitted with a range of wall and floor units, offering ample storage and worktop space. The dining area comfortably accommodates a family table, while the large window enjoys pleasant views over the gardens and the hills.\n\nUtility Room - \nLocated off the kitchen, the utility room provides additional storage and laundry space with access to the rear garden.\n\nMaster Bedroom - \nA spacious double bedroom with fitted wardrobes and the benefit of an en suite shower room.\n\nEn-Suite - \nFitted with a corner shower, WC and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA bright double bedroom overlooking the front garden.\n\nBedroom 3 - \nA well-proportioned bedroom overlooking the rear garden.\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nA spacious family bathroom fitted with a bath, WC and wash hand basin.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Charming detached three-bedroom bungalow</li><li> Detached garage with excellent storage or workshop potential</li><li> Beautifully maintained throughout</li><li> Mature landscaped gardens with generous parking</li><li> Peaceful elevated setting with excellent privacy</li><li> Beautiful countryside, lake and Twelve Bens views</li><li> Principal bedroom with en suite</li><li> Bright, well-proportioned accommodation</li><li> Excellent opportunity to modernise and personalise</li><li> Ideally located between Rosmuck, Cashel, Cill Chiaráin and Carna</li><li> Approximately 10 minutes from Cill Chiaráin</li><li> An ideal permanent residence, holiday home or investment property</ul>"
      },
      {
